        <body>
            <div xml:id="d179">

                <pb facs="0258" n="158" xml:id="pg158"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/24415: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Piedras Negras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Blocker</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Eagle Pass, Tex.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-31T12:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 31,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received 4:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Villa left Sabinas yesterday afternoon marching overland to Barroterán with full
                    force of 700 men where he will entrain troops for Torreón probably stopping one
                    or two days at Cuatro Ciénegas. Authentic report received last night indicates
                    that surrender complete, that Villa will be given command of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">rurales</hi> in State of Chihuahua retaining 200 picked
                    men and the remainder being disbanded or merged into regular army at their will.
                    Depredations at Sabinas estimated that [<hi rendition="#italic">at</hi>] 30,000
                    pesos in the form of forced loans to pay troops, Government guarantees to return
                    same. Am informed that 80 horses were taken from American ranches in vicinity of
                    Sabinas. Villa should arrive Torreón coming Wednesday. Embassy advised.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Blocker</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
